PURPOSE
-------
This file reconciles manuscript-facing numerical tables, figures, recovered
study tables, computational artifacts, and verification evidence.

Its purpose is to ensure that no manuscript table or figure is interpreted
as independently verified COMSOL execution output unless the corresponding
underlying computational artifact has been recovered and verified.

This file is a reconciliation layer between:

    source data
        ↓
    patient-specific geometry
        ↓
    FEM model
        ↓
    mesh
        ↓
    solver execution
        ↓
    gravity/sensitivity simulation
        ↓
    raw numerical output
        ↓
    derived summary tables
        ↓
    figures
        ↓
    manuscript claims


EVIDENCE PRINCIPLE
------------------
The following categories must remain distinct:

1. MODEL SPECIFICATION
   Describes the intended computational framework and parameterization.

2. DOCUMENTED STUDY VALUE
   Numerical value recovered from an existing study table, workbook, note,
   figure source, or extracted project record.

3. DERIVED VALUE
   Numerical value calculated deterministically from documented values.

4. EXECUTION ARTIFACT
   Original or recreated computational output generated by the executed
   COMSOL model.

5. VERIFIED EXECUTION EVIDENCE
   Execution artifact that can be traced to the corresponding model,
   patient, condition, and computational workflow.

A documented study value must not be upgraded to verified execution evidence
without the underlying computational artifact.


