MANUSCRIPT SAFETY RULE
----------------------
Until the computational execution artifacts are recovered or the model is
recreated and executed under a controlled workflow:

Do not use manuscript language such as:

    "all simulations converged"

    "the simulations demonstrated"

    "COMSOL produced"

    "the finite-element analysis showed"

    "mesh independence was achieved"

    "no failed elements were observed"

unless the corresponding execution evidence is available.

Instead use evidence-controlled wording such as:

    "The recovered study records report..."

    "The documented computational results indicate..."

    "The current reconstructed dataset contains..."

    "The normalized response was calculated from the documented summary
     values..."

This distinction must be maintained until Stage-3 verification is complete.


